# EnvironmentFile template for ~/.config/systemd/user/haft.service.
#
# Do NOT copy this file by hand — tools/haft/install.sh renders it into
# ~/.config/axenstax/haft.env (mode 0600) and never overwrites an existing
# one. Three placeholder tokens below are filled in with real, resolved
# paths for this machine at render time: $HOME, $AXENSTAX_PERSONA and
# $AXENSTAX_KITHMOOT_DIR. They are not shell variables systemd expands
# (EnvironmentFile does no variable expansion at all — see
# systemd.exec(5)); install.sh does a plain text substitution before it
# writes the real file, which is why this template is committed and the
# rendered file is not.
#
# After rendering, two lines are still blank and marked REQUIRED — edit the
# rendered file directly, not this template, to fill them in.
#
# Every kithmoot-agent flag can also come from the environment as
# KITHMOOT_<FLAG> (uppercased, dashes to underscores); a command-line flag
# would win, but haft.service passes none beyond --respond, so this file is
# the whole configuration for kithmoot-agent itself. See `kithmoot-agent
# join --help` for every flag. KITHMOOT_DIR below is the one exception: it
# is not a kithmoot-agent flag at all, only something haft.service's own
# ExecStart reads to find the checkout.

# --- where kithmoot lives on this machine --------------------------------

# The kithmoot checkout haft.service runs from
# (${KITHMOOT_DIR}/bin/kithmoot-agent.mjs, already built — see
# tools/haft/README.md). install.sh defaults this to $HOME/kithmoot and
# lets you override with `KITHMOOT_DIR=/path/to/checkout tools/haft/
# install.sh` if yours lives elsewhere.
KITHMOOT_DIR=$AXENSTAX_KITHMOOT_DIR

# --- identity ---------------------------------------------------------

# The participant key file. Already exists at ~/.kithmoot/haft.key (mode
# 0600) — created ahead of this by the owner, never by this unit.
# install.sh REFUSES to render this file if that key is missing,
# specifically so this unit can never be the thing that mints Haft a fresh,
# unrecorded key.
KITHMOOT_IDENTITY=$HOME/.kithmoot/haft.key

# What the room calls Haft.
KITHMOOT_NAME=Haft McHafty

# Pins the identity above to a specific key, so a moved/missing/replaced
# KITHMOOT_IDENTITY file fails loudly instead of quietly minting a fresh key
# that then runs indistinguishably from the real Haft. This is
# KITHMOOT_EXPECT_PUBKEY, not documented in `kithmoot-agent --help`'s env
# list but read the same way as every other flag (KITHMOOT_<FLAG>) —
# confirmed by reading kithmoot's src/node/cli.ts directly, not assumed.
# Fill this in with Haft's own npub once you have it (tools/haft/README.md
# shows how); leave blank only until then.
KITHMOOT_EXPECT_PUBKEY=

# --- the room -----------------------------------------------------------

# REQUIRED. The room link Haft joins. Does not exist until a keeper is
# running somewhere (see tools/haft/README.md) — the room is Phase 6/9 of
# the world-chat build, Haft is Phase 8. Leave this blank and the unit will
# start, log the missing link, and exit; systemd will retry it forever
# (Restart=always) until this is filled in, which is intended: no busy-loop
# guard is needed because backoff is systemd's job, not this file's.
KITHMOOT_LINK=

# --- the agent, and who it belongs to ------------------------------------

# The character in front of the model. Points at this repo's own copy
# (tools/haft/haft-persona.md), so it's reviewed content like any other
# spec-adjacent doc, not a private copy in ~/.config.
KITHMOOT_PERSONA=$AXENSTAX_PERSONA

# Where Haft's conversation memory accumulates. Already exists, empty.
KITHMOOT_MEMORY=$HOME/.kithmoot/haft

# REQUIRED once minted. The ownership proof from `kithmoot-agent attest`,
# run by the OWNER against their own key — never by this session, never by
# this unit (see tools/haft/README.md for the exact command). Without this,
# Haft still runs, but carries no proof of whose agent it is, which is the
# one thing a room with a child in it must not tolerate silently. Fill this
# in before treating the room as live.
KITHMOOT_OWNER_PROOF=$HOME/.config/axenstax/haft-owner-proof.json

# Family relays for the world's room. Not trotters — trotters is AxeNStax's
# own discovery/sign-in/feedback infrastructure and must never carry a
# family's conversation (docs/foundations/2026-09-05-world-chat.md §4.4).
# Replace with the actual family relay list before going live; kithmoot's
# own default relay list starts with trotters, which is exactly the
# omission this line exists to prevent.
KITHMOOT_RELAYS=wss://nos.lol,wss://relay.primal.net

# --- the brain ------------------------------------------------------------

KITHMOOT_BRAIN=anthropic
KITHMOOT_MODEL=claude-opus-5

# REQUIRED for the anthropic brain. Read by the Anthropic SDK from this
# process's environment — KithMoot itself holds no key and never sees this
# value except by passing it through to the SDK. Leave blank and Haft joins
# on... nothing: the anthropic brain will fail to answer until this is set.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
